From 8e8e207a2edfc71ca3dca870928c10187c81fd08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:02:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): a worker's child of a picked-up creator
 copy gets its owner chat's sub

A worker running another gateway's card from a picked-up copy (kanban_worker_node.import_cards) or a synced
card holds the creator's task_chat_links rows but none of its kanban_notify_subs, which never sync. When that
worker filed a child, resolve_chats found the owner in the local file, so inherit_chats took the copy path:
_copy_delivery copies the creator's matching sub and found none. The child got the unreleased created link but
no sub, so its gateway's hub collector published only the creating worker session (rel: created) and no
shepherd for the owning chat.

Worker-3 evidence 2026-11-12: hub card t_01a1ced43b8a9675 ran on worker-3 as a copy and filed
t_01a1cee93a2ecae6 (creator_chats_resolved without source=replica; link to hub/default/20261111_200009_edbe39;
no kanban_notify_subs row). Worker-4's t_01a1cf56f1fd6e73 (creator copy of hub card t_01a1cf477dece56b) is the
same case.

_copy_delivery now falls back to _owner_delivery (the replica path's exact hub/tui sub, reason create) when no
sub for that chat exists on the child after the copy. A local owner sub is still copied with its delivery
columns, and only once.
